.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt MIRROR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mirror
.Nd mirror internet accounts and services to local disk
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar method
.Op Ar flags
.Ar source
.Ar destdir
.Nm
.Ar method
.Fl h
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
copies what
.Ar source
names into the local directory
.Ar destdir ,
which is created if needed.
The
.Ar method
says what kind of source it is, and what
.Ar source
means: a URL, a server, an account or an item identifier.
Each method has its own
.Ar flags ,
which come after the method name;
.Nm
.Ar method
.Fl h
lists them.
.Pp
Running
.Nm
again with the same arguments brings the copy up to date, or picks up
where an interrupted run stopped.
Downloads are written under a temporary name and renamed into place
once complete, so an interrupted run never leaves a truncated file
behind under the real name.
.Pp
Passwords are read from a file named with
.Fl password-file ,
never from the command line, so they stay out of the process list and
the shell history.
The file holds the password on one line.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm version
prints the version.
.Sh METHODS
.Ss archiveorg
Downloads every file of an Internet Archive item over HTTPS.
.Ar source
is a
.Li https://archive.org/details/ Ns Ar id
or
.Li https://archive.org/download/ Ns Ar id
URL, or the bare
.Ar id .
The files land in
.Ar destdir Ns / Ns Ar id ,
with their md5 checksums verified where the item lists them and their
modification times taken from the item's file listing.
A
.Pa .done
file is written once every file is complete, and a later run skips the
item.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f
Check the item again even if it is marked done.
.El
.Ss ftp
Recursively mirrors a directory, or a single file, of an FTP server.
.Ar source
is
.Sm off
.Li ftp://
.Oo Ar user Op : Ar password
@
.Oc
.Ar host Op : Ar port
.Ar path
.Sm on ,
or
.Li ftps://
for implicit TLS (port 990).
Files land in
.Ar destdir Ns / Ns Ar host Ns / Ns Ar path .
Directories are listed with MLSD where the server supports it, and LIST
otherwise.
Symbolic links that LIST reports are recreated locally.
Interrupted downloads are resumed with REST.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl user Ar name
Log in as
.Ar name .
The default is the user in the URL, or
.Li anonymous .
.It Fl password-file Ar file
Read the password from
.Ar file .
.It Fl tls
Upgrade the connection with AUTH TLS (explicit FTPS).
.It Fl update
List every directory again, and download files whose size or
modification time changed, files that are missing locally, and files
that failed permanently before.
.El
.Ss gopher
Recursively mirrors a Gopher menu tree.
.Ar source
is a
.Li gopher://
URL, such as
.Li gopher:// Ns Ar host Ns Li /1/ Ns Ar menu .
Files land in
.Ar destdir Ns / Ns Ar host Ns / Ns Ar selector ,
and the info lines of each menu in a
.Pa 00README
file.
Only items on the same host and port, below the starting selector, are
followed.
.Ss gphotos
Downloads a Google Photos library in original quality, using the
browser session that
.Fl cookies
holds.
.Ar source
is the account's email address, which is only used for logging.
Files land in
.Ar destdir Ns / Ns Ar YYYY Ns / Ns Ar MM
by the date they were taken.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl cookies Ar file
Cookies for photos.google.com: a Netscape
.Pa cookies.txt
export, or on macOS a
.Pa .binarycookies
file such as Safari's.
The default is
.Pa cookies.txt .
.It Fl after Ar YYYY-MM-DD
Only items taken on or after this date.
.It Fl before Ar YYYY-MM-DD
Only items taken on or before this date.
.It Fl last Ar duration
Only items taken in the last
.Ar duration ,
such as 30d, 2w, 6m or 1y.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl after .
.It Fl companions Ns = Ns Ar bool
Also download the RAW companion of a Pixel RAW+JPEG pair.
On by default.
.El
.Ss groupsio
Downloads every file in a groups.io group's Files section.
.Ar source
is the group's short name, the
.Ar name
in
.Li https://groups.io/g/ Ns Ar name .
Files land in
.Ar destdir Ns / Ns Ar name .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl email Ar address
The groups.io account to log in with.
Required.
.It Fl password-file Ar file
Read the account's password from
.Ar file .
Required.
.El
.Ss http
Recursively mirrors everything under a path of an HTTP or HTTPS server.
.Ar source
is a URL; everything under its directory, after redirects, is mirrored.
Files land in
.Ar destdir Ns / Ns Ar host Ns / Ns Ar path ;
a URL ending in
.Ql /
is saved as
.Pa index.html .
Links are followed only on the same scheme and host and under that
path, but the images, stylesheets and scripts of every saved page are
fetched from wherever they are.
Directory listings generated by the server are only used to find files:
they are not saved, and their sorting links are not followed.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl update
Check everything already mirrored again with conditional requests, read
directory listings again for new files, and retry URLs that failed with
a 4xx status.
.It Fl wait Ar duration
Wait
.Ar duration ,
such as 1s or 500ms, between requests.
.El
.Ss icloud
Downloads iCloud Photos originals.
.Ar source
is the Apple ID.
Signing in may ask for a two-factor code; the session is saved, so
later runs usually don't need the password again.
Files land in
.Ar destdir Ns / Ns Ar YYYY Ns / Ns Ar MM
by the date they were taken.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl password-file Ar file
Read the Apple ID password from
.Ar file .
Only needed when there is no valid saved session.
.It Fl session-dir Ar dir
Where to save the session.
The default is a directory per account under the user's cache
directory.
.It Fl album Ar name
The album to mirror.
The default is
.Dq All Photos .
.It Fl live-photo-video Ns = Ns Ar bool
Also download the video of a Live Photo.
On by default.
.It Fl after , Fl before , Fl last
As for
.Sx gphotos .
.El
.Ss imap
Mirrors the mail of an IMAP account, one Maildir per folder.
.Ar source
is
.Ar host
or
.Sm off
.Ar host : Ar port ;
.Sm on
the connection always uses TLS, on port 993 by default.
Each folder lands in
.Ar destdir Ns / Ns Ar folder ,
following the server's folder hierarchy.
Messages already present are not downloaded again.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl user Ar name
The account to log in as.
Required.
.It Fl password-file Ar file
Read the account's password from
.Ar file .
Required.
.It Fl mailbox Ar folder
Mirror only
.Ar folder ,
directly into
.Ar destdir .
.El
.Ss rsync
Mirrors an rsync source in archive mode, like
.Ic rsync -a .
.Ar source
is
.Sm off
.Li rsync:// Op Ar user @
.Ar host Op : Ar port
.Li / Ar module Op / Ar path
.Sm on
or
.Sm off
.Op Ar user @
.Ar host :: Ar module Op / Ar path
.Sm on
for an rsync daemon (anonymous modules only), or
.Sm off
.Op Ar user @
.Ar host : Ar path
.Sm on
over
.Xr ssh 1 .
As with
.Xr rsync 1 ,
.Ar destdir
is the destination itself, and a trailing slash on the source path
copies the directory's contents rather than the directory.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl delete
Delete local files that no longer exist on the remote side.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev ICLOUD_PASSWORD
The Apple ID password for
.Sx icloud ,
if
.Fl password-file
is not given.
.It Ev RSYNC_RSH
The remote shell
.Sx rsync
runs for a
.Sm off
.Ar host : Ar path
.Sm on
source, instead of
.Xr ssh 1 .
.El
.Sh FILES
The state that lets a later run continue is kept in
.Ar destdir :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa .httpmirror.db , .ftpmirror.db
SQLite databases of every URL or file seen by
.Sx http
and
.Sx ftp ,
and whether it is done.
.It Pa .gphotos-index.json , .icloud-index.json
The items already downloaded by
.Sx gphotos
and
.Sx icloud .
.It Ar id Ns Pa /.done
An Internet Archive item that
.Sx archiveorg
has completely downloaded.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 if everything was mirrored, 1 if anything failed, and 2 for a
usage error.
A failed run can be repeated: it continues with what is not done yet.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mirror a directory of a web server:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mirror http https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/hello/ ~/mirror
.Ed
.Pp
Mirror an FTP tree, then later pick up new and changed files:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mirror ftp ftp://ftp.example.com/pub/ ~/mirror
mirror ftp -update ftp://ftp.example.com/pub/ ~/mirror
.Ed
.Pp
Mirror a mail account:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mirror imap -user me@example.com -password-file ~/.imap-pw \e
    imap.example.com ~/mail
.Ed
.Pp
Download an Internet Archive item:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mirror archiveorg https://archive.org/details/some-item ~/archive
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rsync 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr wget 1
.Pp
The README of each method, in
.Pa /usr/share/doc/mirrortools
(or
.Pa /usr/local/share/mirrortools
on macOS) and at
.Lk https://github.com/rpajarola/mirrortools .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Rico Pajarola Aq Mt rp@servium.ch
